      "writtenOn": "2026-04-20T07:37:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can definitely see that perspective, I thought about it for a while myself.\n\nMy issue with that is that there\u0027s a massive user experience difference between telling the user:\n```\nsuggestion: add [ \":baz\" ] to the public_deps of \"//foo:bar\"\n```\n\nAnd telling the user:\n```\nsuggestion: run `gn refs \u003coutput directory\u003e foo/baz.h`, strip the toolchain, ensure there\u0027s only one, and add that as a public_dep of \"//foo:bar\n```\n\nAlso, `gn refs` basically just reruns most of the work of `gn gen` each time you run it, and I\u0027ve seen it output hundreds of these errors at once. This provides a fast, indexable way to do it. Although it\u0027s only being used for chromium currently, strict deps could in theory be used by anyone.\n\nIf you\u0027d like, we can lock it behind a gn arg instead?",
      "parentUuid": "422aa963_881a3642",
      "revId": "f042becd9bec40ac3f1017b72cc85b7da38aad62",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf3a7dfe_232c7910",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000030
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-21T03:00:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Considering that we can ask this kind of repetetive work to ai agent now, I think such difference is not a large problem if suggestion is understandable to ai. And I still think having this feature in GN is too specific to chromium and layer violation.\n\nIf running `gn refs` multiple times are problematic, we can pass multiple headers to the command to get targets including those headers.",
      "parentUuid": "0130680e_238ff72a",
      "revId": "f042becd9bec40ac3f1017b72cc85b7da38aad62",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
